## Tool versions and updates

The development tools are pinned in `pyproject.toml` to versions tested with
these configurations. Run them from this project's environment. Ruff's
`required-version` rejects a different version. Editor extensions may ship
their own tools; use the project environment where supported and run the
pinned command-line checks before committing.

`.womm-template.json` records the generator, template version and original
choices. It is provenance, not a list of the tools currently installed.

To upgrade a tool, change its dependency pin and any matching version guard,
review its release notes, and update its configuration if needed.
{% if use_uv %}Run `uv lock` and `uv sync --locked --group dev`, then run all quality,
test and build checks before committing the updated configuration and lockfile.
{% else %}Reinstall with `python -m pip install -e . --group dev`, then run all
quality, test and build checks. Exact tool pins do not lock transitive
dependencies; use a separate constraints workflow if you need a fully locked
pip environment.
{% endif %}Upgrading WOMM does not update this project's files.

